      "message": "Hi Andrew,\n\nCould you take a look what I missed here that when running `atest libavmd_test`, I always get the following output?\n\n```\nRunning Tests...\n\narm64-v8a libavmd_test\n----------------------\navmdtool (0 Tests)\nRUNNER ERROR: test did not report any run:\nerror: Found argument \u0027-Z\u0027 which wasn\u0027t expected, or isn\u0027t valid in this context\n\nUSAGE:\navmdtool \u003cSUBCOMMAND\u003e\n\nFor more information try --help\n\n\n\narm64-v8a libavmd_test\n----------------------\nlibavmd_test (1 Test)\n[1/1] libavmd_test#test_dump: PASSED (27ms)\n\nSummary (Test executed with 1 devices.)\n-------\narm64-v8a libavmd_test: Passed: 0, Failed: 0, Ignored: 0, Assumption Failed: 0,   (Completed With ERRORS) \narm64-v8a libavmd_test: Passed: 1, Failed: 0, Ignored: 0, Assumption Failed: 0,    \n\n1 test failed\n```\nWhy there is always the `avmdtool` part?\n\nThanks!",
